# Nothing reloads when windows open and close, focus moves or a notification
# arrives (latency.md step 6). The desktop widgets' area must not change in
# the recordings (static), and with TESSERA_PERF the Rust log has no
# `debug: reload` line for these. (Widgets at 30,50 720x540 at 1x: check
# against the first shot and adjust if the user's layout differs.)
look material
ptr move 1000 700
wait 2
shot desktop-start
# a terminal opens (ALT + Return), and a second
rec open-window 2.5 key -M alt -k Return -m alt
static widgets-open-window 30 50 720 540
rec open-second 2.5 key -M alt -k Return -m alt
static widgets-open-second 30 50 720 540
shot two-windows
# the focused one closes (ALT + F4)
rec close-window 2.0 key -M alt -k F4 -m alt
static widgets-close-window 30 50 720 540
# focus moves to the other by a click on it
rec focus-click 1.5 ptr move 1300 500 click
static widgets-focus 30 50 720 540
# a notification arrives (sent from inside the recording's single step: by
# the shell's own test call)
setup sleep 0.3; notify-send -a Files 'Copied' '3 files' &
rec notification 2.5 ptr move 1300 520
static widgets-notification 30 50 720 540
# panels open and close over the desktop
rec nc-open 1.6 ipc panels open notificationCenter TESSERA-TEST
rec nc-close 1.4 ipc panels close
static widgets-nc 30 50 720 540
rec overview-open 1.6 ipc panels open overview TESSERA-TEST
rec overview-close 1.4 ipc panels close
rec mc-open 1.6 ipc panels open missionControl TESSERA-TEST
rec mc-close 1.4 ipc panels close
static widgets-mc 30 50 720 540
# the last window goes
rec close-last 2.0 key -M alt -k F4 -m alt
static widgets-close-last 30 50 720 540
note every static check holds; `grep "debug: reload" tessera-ui.log` lists nothing for these steps (Rust)
